{#- #620, 10 Sep 2026; rewritten by #830, reshaped by #838 (28 Sep) and moved
    onto the shared shape by #841 (29 Sep). The page Close's integration
    directory points at (close.com/integrations/prospektor) and the answer to
    two required fields on their listing form (#9 Marketing URL, and "do you
    promote Close on your website in any way?").

    THE SHAPE is `_includes/integration-page.njk`, Close's own integration
    page: a back link and the mark, the name as the <h1> with the fit sentence
    under it, a sidebar with the one action and the way into the help, two
    visuals, three paragraphs, three steps. This page adds one thing the
    others do not: the direct-to-Stripe card (`intExtra`), because the free
    month is sold here and nowhere else (#622).

    THE ONE THING THIS PAGE MUST NOT DO: sell whom to chase. Its visitor
    already has a CRM and already believes in it. Everything here is the half
    Close does not have, and where it lands when it is done.

    Every claim here is the studio's code, read on 28 Sep 2026, and if one of
    them stops being true this page is wrong, not modest:
      - the one-press connect is the Close OAuth app (#582/#583, live since
        `6aa20f8` on the studio), so no key is pasted;
      - what a push writes is `lib/crm-close.js` (#582, proven in production
        by the operator's own press on 10 Sep): the lead found by domain, its
        contacts, an opportunity whose CONFIDENCE is the fit score, and a
        note that renders; a second press updates by id.

    THE OFFER IS WRITTEN ONLY WHEN THIS BUILD ARMS IT (#622). Every sentence
    that says "free", "30 days" or "$0" sits inside `{% if offer.close %}`, so
    the page cannot promise a month the checkout call would not grant, and the
    dark build is the same page at list price. `test/close.test.js` builds
    both and reads every "N days" against `lib/trial.js`. -#}

